===Etymology===
{{unk|en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɪl.tʃəd/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɪl.t͡ʃɚd/|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|pilchard|s}}

# Any of various small [[oily]] [[fish]] related to [[herring]]s, family {{taxfmt|Clupeidae|family}}.
#* '''1839''', John Hookham Frere (translator), ''The Birds'', lines 76–77, in ''Acharnians and two other plays''
#*: He longs occasionally for human diet,<br />His old Athenian fare: '''pilchards''', for instance.

====Usage notes====
The terms ''sardine'' and ''pilchard'' are not precise, and what is meant depends on the region. Often, the smaller fish are termed ''sardines'' and the larger ones ''pilchards''.

